course: dictionary
lesson: 2431
title: A small bird that dives
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dabchick is a small water bird. «A dabchick is the little grebe, a small bird that dives for its food.» The sentence tells you what it is and what it does, so you can work out the meaning without a dictionary.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Otters, kingfishers, dabchicks, moorhens» is a list of creatures on a river bank, so a dabchick lives near water. Try your meaning in the sentence: «a small water bird that dives for its food» still makes sense, so you are probably right.
explain: Dabchicks are hard to spot. They dive so quickly that they seem to vanish, and they often swim with only their head showing. Their toes are lobed, not webbed like a duck's, and they build nests that float on the water.
fact: Dabchick is another name for the little grebe.
fact: A dabchick is a small water bird that dives under water to catch small fish and insects.
fact: A dabchick often swims with only its head showing above the water.
fact: Old books also use «dabchick» for some other small grebes.
fact: Grebes have lobed toes, not webbed toes, and build floating nests.
exercise: «A dabchick is a small bird that dives for its food.» What does a dabchick do to find food? | Eats only plants | Flies high over the trees | Digs a tunnel in the river bank | *Dives under water to catch fish and insects
exercise: Dabchick is another name for which bird? | Otter | Moorhen | *Little grebe | Kingfisher
exercise: «The dabchick dived so quickly it seemed to vanish.» What does vanish mean? | *Disappear suddenly | Sing loudly | Appear | Fall asleep
test: «Often a dabchick swims with only its head showing.» What can you see above the water? | Its wings | Its feet | *Its head | Its tail
test: Which word is an old name used for some other small grebes? | Moorhen | Otter | Kingfisher | *Dabchick
exam: Which sentence best tells you what a dabchick is? | A dabchick is a boat used to cross the river. | *A dabchick is a small water bird that dives under water to catch fish. | A dabchick is a large animal that lives in a cave. | A dabchick is a tree that grows beside the river.
